A||N||6||Calab52||Steering Wheel Movement.||||11||
Z||000000||Calab52||09-23-2001||10:53 PM||||Can someone explain why my steering wheel moves back and forth? Is something loose? How can I fix this?||||reg||11
Z||000001||terryk||09-24-2001||12:11 AM||||It's designed to move back and forth. This allows you to steer the car by rotating the wheel thus the term "steering wheel".<P>Ok, it could be the rack/pinion is worn or the outer tie-rods. Get someone to rock the steering wheel while you check the outer tie-rods for movement. Ten bucks the rack is worn. If so, you should get a rebuild and new outer tie-rods (seperate item).<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||09-24-2001||12:17 AM||||More common if the wheel "jiggles" then its simply (I say simply, not all that simple) the 4 bolts inside the steering colum. I had to fix it on my Formula, but its been over a year and I dont remember much about it. If I recall you take off the steering wheel and some of the guts inside the colum, move the wiring to the side, and you'll see 4 bolts...tighten them up and it'll be like new. This is more than likely the solution, provided you've got the problem Im thinking about....its another common Fiero problem.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||09-24-2001||11:26 AM||||There have been lots of past posts/how to on this one if you can get the right search words.  Sounds pretty straightforward but like many Fieroisms, it's a PITA.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000004||falconhulk||09-24-2001||11:32 AM||||Very common problem with GM cars!!  I had this happen to my tilt stering in my firebird and followed Fiero instructions to fix it.  It seems to be from perople grabbing the stering wheel when climbing in.  Its a 30 second fix with 1 1/2 hours of pulling crap apart the first time.  After you do this the first time it will take you only 30 minutes on any other GM car.  Use Loctite on the threads so this does not happen again and try not to let anyone use your wheel to balance when getting in.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-4_b_l.jpg">  <BR>85 SE||||reg||1
Z||000005||deceler8||09-24-2001||11:43 AM||||Before you tear the column apart, take off the horn pad and check that the torx screws holding the wheel to the hub are tight.<P>These do loosen and can cause the slop you're referring to.||||reg||1
Z||000006||NEPTUNE||09-24-2001||11:49 AM||||Detailed instructions avail. [www.anglefire.com/biz/fierosfierosails/<BR>or search for "fiero sail panels"<BR>lots of good how- too stuff here.<p>[This message has been edited by NEPTUNE (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||4
